# cmd reads a batch file by byte offset and needs the carriage returns to
# find the end of a line. Without them it runs as far as the first goto and
# then executes fragments of its own comments -- which is how four of the
# five batch files here ended up unable to build anything.
#
# The pre-commit check refuses one that slips through; this stops git being
# the thing that converts them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
